Game itself is really fun and nice to pass time, but as space operas and strategies there are better ones out there 6/10
My experience is with free trial weekend, never played game before but played Endless space 1;
Game works fine, plays fine and up to a certain point even looks nice. Technically it's same Endless Space 1, but with minor changes in political system and exploration. After few playtroughts I feel confident to write this. My own biggest dissapointment comes from ''space battles'' where they are technically paperdolls of spaceships shooting eachother for few seconds untill one after another explodes in very dull and boring way. Idea is dragged from first game (which is pretty good in my opinion) but battles are not inpactful and visually unimpressive. In trailers I saw big and impressive battles with cool effects, but in reality it is very uninpactful and boring to watch. It's 2017 guys, in year 2000 it would have been impressive, but now it's an insult to eyes.

Pros:
- EXCELLENT Storyline;
- The ambientation and references are extremelly precise, you really feel 50's L.A.;
- Strong character building;
- Game is very immersive;
Cons:
- Some bugs (walking, driving, etc);
- If you do not understand the languages offered in the game, you will possibly lose important details in the story;
- Some investigations are long (not a con if you enjoy the game).
Rating: 100/100 - A TRUE MASTERPIECE.
